WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.875
Unit 1 is the guide's gate.

2
00:00:01.875 --> 00:00:07.293
Its Step 5 is the program's guidance:
build the target, give it two human owners,

3
00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:12.625
run old and new in parallel for thirty
days, then disable the legacy account.

4
00:00:12.625 --> 00:00:13.725
Never delete it.

5
00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:16.359
Step 2 adds the
prerequisites for a G M S A.

6
00:00:16.359 --> 00:00:21.626
Microsoft Learn's page on creating a K D S
root key says the key is created once per

7
00:00:21.626 --> 00:00:24.978
domain, and domain controllers
wait up to ten hours

8
00:00:24.978 --> 00:00:27.772
after it's created before
they allow a G M S A.

9
00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:32.401
Step 3's seventh step covers the
Active Directory side of credentials:

10
00:00:32.401 --> 00:00:38.147
Learn's guidance on securing group managed
service accounts says Windows changes the

11
00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:40.701
password every thirty days by default,

12
00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:44.612
and the interval can be set only
when the account is created.

13
00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:47.535
The rollback for Step 5 is
to re-enable the legacy

14
00:00:47.535 --> 00:00:50.750
account and revert the
application's configuration.

15
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.467
A delegated account runs
the same thirty days:

16
00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:58.329
Learn's overview of delegated managed
service accounts recommends waiting four

17
00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:02.261
ticket lifetimes, and thirty days
covers four seven-day lifetimes,

18
00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:05.110
so the program completes
a migration only then.
